msgid "# AI Code Review"
msgstr "# AI 代码审查"

msgid ""
"The AI review agent provides deep, on-demand code review for pull requests. "
"It complements — never replaces — human review: first-pass screening "
"(CODEOWNERS routing, gemini-code-assist comments) and CI run automatically "
"on every PR, while the AI review agent handles the deep rounds that a "
"reviewer explicitly requests. The agent can never approve or merge; its "
"verdict is advisory input for the human reviewer."
msgstr ""
"AI 审查 agent 为 pull request 提供深入的按需代码审查。它补充——而非取代——人工审查：第一轮筛查（CODEOWNERS "
"路由、gemini-code-assist 评论）和 CI 会在每个 PR 上自动运行，而 AI 审查 agent 负责处理审查者明确请求的深度轮次。该"
" agent 永远不能批准或合并；其结论仅作为人工审查者的参考输入。"

msgid ""
"The mechanism was proposed in [RFC #21451](https://github.com/vllm-"
"project/vllm-ascend/issues/21451) and is currently in a **gray release** "
"(limited reviewers, opt-in per PR)."
msgstr ""
"该机制在 [RFC #21451](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/issues/21451) "
"中提出，目前处于**灰度发布**阶段（限定审查者，按 PR 选择加入）。"

msgid "## How it works, end to end"
msgstr "## 端到端工作原理"

msgid "### Triggering and the gray-release gate"
msgstr "### 触发方式与灰度发布门禁"

msgid "### Review rounds"
msgstr "### 审查轮次"

msgid "### Multi-round interaction and termination"
msgstr "### 多轮交互与终止"

msgid ""
"The bot updates one PR summary comment. Its hidden `ai-review-state` JSON "
"block records the reviewed commit, published rounds and finding history. A "
"round counts when the bot publishes its result or a notice that the code "
"changed during review. If a run fails before publication, a rerun starts a "
"fresh review from the last published summary."
msgstr ""
"bot 只更新同一条 PR 摘要评论。其隐藏的 `ai-review-state` JSON 块记录已审查的 commit、已发布的轮次和发现项历史。当"
" bot "
"发布审查结果，或发布“审查期间代码已变更”的通知时，该轮次才计入统计。如果某次运行在发布之前失败，重跑将从最近一次已发布的摘要开始一次全新的审查。"

msgid "| Event | Effect |"
msgstr "| 事件 | 影响 |"

msgid ""
"| Author pushes a commit | Revoke `ai-review-passed`. The next `/ai-review` "
"reviews all changes together. |"
msgstr "| 作者推送 commit | 撤销 `ai-review-passed`。下一次 `/ai-review` 会一并审查所有变更。 |"

msgid ""
"| Review covers the full diff, no MUST-FIX remains open and no human "
"decision is pending | The orchestrator applies `ai-review-passed`. |"
msgstr ""
"| 审查覆盖完整 diff、没有未解决的 MUST-FIX，且没有待定的人工决策 | 编排器添加 `ai-review-passed`。 |"

msgid ""
"| Round cap reached (5 per commit) | Push changes and request review again, "
"or ask an allowlisted reviewer to restart the session. |"
msgstr "| 达到轮次上限（每个 commit 5 轮） | 推送变更并再次请求审查，或请白名单中的审查者重启会话。 |"

msgid ""
"| Session budget exhausted (15 published rounds) | An allowlisted reviewer "
"can remove and reapply the label to reset both counts. Existing findings are"
" retained. |"
msgstr "| 会话预算耗尽（已发布 15 轮） | 白名单中的审查者可以移除并重新添加标签，以重置两个计数。已有的发现项会保留。 |"

msgid ""
"Each PR allows one running review job and one pending job. When another "
"authorized request enters a full queue, it replaces the pending job."
msgstr "每个 PR 允许存在一个正在运行的审查任务和一个待处理任务。当另一个已授权的请求进入已满的队列时，它会替换掉待处理任务。"

msgid ""
"`ai-review-passed` is **not an approve**. Human review remains the merge "
"gate."
msgstr "`ai-review-passed` **并不是批准**。人工审查仍然是合并的门禁。"

msgid "## For PR authors"
msgstr "## 面向 PR 作者"

msgid "## Knowledge base maintenance"
msgstr "## 知识库维护"

msgid ""
"The review rules live in `.github/agent-review/` and follow the project's "
"ownership model — the people who own a module own the review rules for it:"
msgstr "审查规则位于 `.github/agent-review/` 下，并遵循项目的归属模型——拥有某个模块的人同时拥有该模块的审查规则："

msgid ""
"- **Ownership is enforced by CODEOWNERS.** Each `L2/<domain>/` directory gets one CODEOWNERS entry naming that domain's owners (later entries win over the `/.github` wildcard). Editing a domain's rules then requires those owners' approval — the same gate as editing the code itself.\n"
"- **Updating rules** is an ordinary PR against the checklist file. Changes are effective for the next review round; there is no deployment step.\n"
"- **Adding a domain** takes three steps: create `L2/<domain>/checklist.md` with stable rule IDs (`L2-<domain>#slug`), add a coarse glob entry to `domains.yaml`, append the CODEOWNERS entry. Keep domains coarse — per-file directories are explicitly avoided.\n"
"- **Rule discipline**: rule IDs are stable API (findings cite them); every rule must be decidable from the diff and repository files (things needing test runs or hardware belong to human review); explicitly exclude what the agent should not report."
msgstr ""
"- **归属由 CODEOWNERS 强制执行。** 每个 `L2/<domain>/` 目录对应一条 CODEOWNERS 条目，指定该领域的负责人（靠后的条目优先于 `/.github` 通配符）。因此编辑某个领域的规则需要这些负责人批准——与编辑代码本身的门禁相同。\n"
"- **更新规则**是针对 checklist 文件的普通 PR。变更将在下一轮审查中生效，无需部署步骤。\n"
"- **新增领域**需要三个步骤：创建含稳定规则 ID（`L2-<domain>#slug`）的 `L2/<domain>/checklist.md`，在 `domains.yaml` 中添加一条粗粒度的 glob 条目，追加 CODEOWNERS 条目。领域应保持粗粒度——明确避免按文件划分目录。\n"
"- **规则纪律**：规则 ID 是稳定的 API（发现项会引用它们）；每条规则都必须能根据 diff 和仓库文件判定（需要运行测试或依赖硬件的应归入人工审查）；明确排除 agent 不应报告的内容。"

msgid ""
"During the gray release, maintainer feedback on the agent's inline comments "
"(agree/disagree/corrections) is the main input for checklist iteration. "
"Collect it and land checklist updates in small weekly batches rather than "
"one change per finding."
msgstr ""
"灰度发布期间，维护者对 agent 行内评论的反馈（同意 / 不同意 / "
"纠正）是检查清单迭代的主要输入。请收集这些反馈，并以每周小批量的方式提交检查清单更新，而不是每发现一个问题就修改一次。"

msgid "## Components"
msgstr "## 组件"

msgid "| Path | Role |"
msgstr "| 路径 | 作用 |"

msgid ""
"| `.github/workflows/ai_review.yml` | trigger orchestration (label / comment"
" / push), gates, agent job on the self-hosted CPU pool |"
msgstr ""
"| `.github/workflows/ai_review.yml` | 触发编排（标签 / 评论 / push）、门禁，以及在自托管 CPU "
"资源池上运行的 agent 任务 |"

msgid ""
"| `.github/workflows/scripts/ai_review.py` | state machine, prompt assembly,"
" finding parsing, inline comment posting |"
msgstr "| `.github/workflows/scripts/ai_review.py` | 状态机、提示词组装、问题解析、行内评论发布 |"

msgid ""
"| `.github/workflows/dockerfiles/Dockerfile.ai-review` | preinstalled agent "
"image (Node + dsh CLI) |"
msgstr ""
"| `.github/workflows/dockerfiles/Dockerfile.ai-review` | 预装 agent 的镜像（Node +"
" dsh CLI） |"

msgid ""
"| `.github/workflows/_schedule_ai_review_image_build.yaml` | image build "
"workflow (Dockerfile changes or manual dispatch) |"
msgstr ""
"| `.github/workflows/_schedule_ai_review_image_build.yaml` | "
"镜像构建工作流（Dockerfile 变更或手动触发） |"

msgid ""
"| `.github/agent-review/` | instructions, knowledge base, allowlist, domain "
"registry |"
msgstr "| `.github/agent-review/` | 指令、知识库、允许列表、领域注册表 |"

msgid ""
"The agent engine is deliberately decoupled: the orchestrator invokes a "
"configurable command (a repository variable), so the underlying engine can "
"be replaced without workflow surgery."
msgstr "agent 引擎有意做了解耦：编排器调用一个可配置的命令（仓库变量），因此无需改动工作流即可替换底层引擎。"

msgid "### Documentation changes"
msgstr "### 文档变更"

msgid ""
"When the current PR diff changes either root README (`README.md` or "
"`README.zh.md`), Markdown in `docs/` or `vllm_ascend/ops/triton/docs/`, or "
"Chinese translations in `docs/source/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/`, the agent "
"reviews the documentation against internal standards and reports "
"documentation findings alongside code findings in the same round."
msgstr ""
"当当前 PR 的 diff 改动了根目录 README（`README.md` 或 `README.zh.md`）、`docs/` 或 "
"`vllm_ascend/ops/triton/docs/` 中的 Markdown，或 "
"`docs/source/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/` "
"中的中文翻译时，智能体将依据内部标准审查文档，并在同一轮中与代码问题一并报告文档问题。"

msgid ""
"- An operator listed in `.github/agent-review/allowlist.txt` can start a review by applying the `ai-review` label to a PR. Applying the label requires permission to manage PR labels on GitHub. If an unlisted person applies it, the bot posts a notice and removes the label.\n"
"- Once enabled, any listed operator can request another review, waive findings, or stop the review by commenting on the PR. The same list applies to PR authors and maintainers. To join the pilot, comment on RFC #21451.\n"
"- During the gray release the agent's PR comments are posted by the maintainer's bot account, with the summary headed **AI review · DeepSeek Harness headless · POC pilot**. The bot appends an Actions link to accepted command comments and explains rejections on the original comment."
msgstr ""
"- 只有列入 `.github/agent-review/allowlist.txt` 的操作者才能通过为 PR 添加 `ai-review` 标签来启动评审。添加该标签需要具备在 GitHub 上管理 PR 标签的权限。如果未列入名单的人添加了该标签，机器人会发布通知并移除该标签。\n"
"- 一旦启用，名单中的任何操作者都可以通过评论 PR 来请求再次评审、豁免问题或停止评审。同一份名单同样适用于 PR 作者和 maintainer。如需加入试点，请在 RFC #21451 下评论。\n"
"- 在灰度发布期间，agent 的 PR 评论由 maintainer 的机器人账号发布，摘要标题为 **AI review · DeepSeek Harness headless · POC pilot**。机器人会在已接受的命令评论后追加 Actions 链接，并在原评论中说明拒绝原因。"

msgid ""
"Each round is one agent invocation. The prompt includes the following "
"information."
msgstr "每一轮都是一次 agent 调用。提示词包含以下信息。"

msgid ""
"1. The path to the trusted project guidelines, the knowledge-base map and the domains the PR touches.\n"
"2. The PR title and description, target branch tip, merge base, head and `git diff --stat`.\n"
"3. The last published review's head, merge base, coverage status and summary, plus a separate list of unfinished static checks.\n"
"4. Open and resolved findings, waived findings and their reasons, the triggering comment (if any) and the expected review format."
msgstr ""
"1. 可信项目指南的路径、知识库地图，以及该 PR 涉及的领域。\n"
"2. PR 的标题和描述、目标分支的最新提交、合并基点、head 以及 `git diff --stat`。\n"
"3. 上次发布的评审所对应的 head、合并基点、覆盖状态和摘要，以及一份单独列出的未完成静态检查清单。\n"
"4. 未关闭和已解决的问题、已豁免的问题及其原因、触发评论（如有）以及期望的评审格式。"

msgid ""
"The agent runs in a Git worktree at the reviewed head and uses Git to "
"inspect changes from the merge base. It reads applicable checklists from the"
" trusted checkout. After about ten minutes, it is asked to finish with the "
"evidence it has. The workflow stops the agent after twelve minutes."
msgstr ""
"agent 在被评审的 head 所对应的 Git worktree 中运行，并使用 Git "
"检查自合并基点以来的变更。它会从可信检出中读取适用的检查清单。大约十分钟后，系统会要求它基于已有证据收尾。工作流会在十二分钟后停止 agent。"

msgid ""
"The review summary explains what the agent checked, what it concluded and "
"which claims still need runtime evidence. A separate list names the static "
"checks left for the next round. A round with unfinished checks cannot pass. "
"An allowlisted operator can comment `/ai-review` to continue those checks "
"and review any new changes. A completed review has an empty list and keeps "
"its summary for the next round."
msgstr ""
"评审摘要会说明 agent "
"检查了什么、得出了什么结论，以及哪些论断仍需要运行时证据。另有一份单独的清单列出留待下一轮完成的静态检查。存在未完成检查的轮次无法通过。名单中的操作者可以评论"
" `/ai-review` 来继续这些检查并评审任何新变更。已完成的评审其清单为空，并保留摘要供下一轮使用。"

msgid ""
"If you withdraw a documentation change, include the reason and finding ID in"
" the next review request. The agent can mark that finding `resolved` after "
"verifying the affected content was withdrawn. If you moved the content and "
"the issue persists, the finding stays open."
msgstr ""
"如果你撤回了某处文档修改，请在下次评审请求中说明原因和问题 ID。agent 在确认受影响的内容已被撤回后，可以将该问题标记为 "
"`resolved`。如果你只是移动了内容而问题依然存在，该问题将保持未关闭状态。"

msgid ""
"Waivers, stop commands and discarded results can update the comment. The "
"next review still receives the snapshot, summary and unfinished checks from "
"the last round that published a review result."
msgstr "豁免、停止命令和被丢弃的结果都可能更新该评论。下一次评审仍会收到最后一次发布评审结果的轮次所提供的快照、摘要和未完成检查。"

msgid ""
"| Allowlisted operator comments `/ai-review` | Request one review of the "
"current PR. Include explanations for multiple findings in the same top-level"
" comment. |"
msgstr "| 名单中的操作者评论 `/ai-review` | 请求对当前 PR 进行一次评审。若涉及多个问题，请在同一条顶层评论中一并说明。 |"

msgid ""
"| Allowlisted operator comments `/ai-review-waive F003 reason` or `/ai-"
"review-waive all reason` | Permanently waive one or all open finding IDs on "
"this PR. Existing inline comments show `[WAIVED by @user]`. The bot updates "
"the verdict without calling the agent. |"
msgstr ""
"| 名单中的操作者评论 `/ai-review-waive F003 reason` 或 `/ai-review-waive all reason` |"
" 永久豁免此 PR 上的一个或全部未关闭问题 ID。已有的行内评论会显示 `[WAIVED by @user]`。机器人会在不调用 agent "
"的情况下更新判定结果。 |"

msgid ""
"| Someone removes the label on GitHub, or an allowlisted operator comments "
"`/ai-review-stop` | Stop review and remove both labels. Wait for the Stop "
"workflow to finish before reapplying `ai-review`. |"
msgstr ""
"| 有人在 GitHub 上移除标签，或名单中的操作者评论 `/ai-review-stop` | 停止评审并移除两个标签。请等待 Stop "
"工作流结束后再重新添加 `ai-review`。 |"

msgid ""
"Waived IDs stay archived in the PR summary after a push. Before reporting a "
"new problem, the agent consults the waiver list to avoid repeating a "
"behavior and impact the reviewer already accepted. A distinct defect or an "
"impact outside the waiver can receive a new ID, even on the same line."
msgstr ""
"推送之后，已豁免的 ID 仍会归档在 PR 摘要中。在报告新问题之前，agent "
"会查阅豁免清单，避免重复评审者已经接受的行为和影响。不同的缺陷或超出豁免范围的影响可以获得新的 ID，即使出现在同一行。"

msgid ""
"When new evidence changes an open or resolved finding's impact, the agent "
"can raise or lower its severity under the same ID. The bot updates the "
"original inline comment and uses the new severity for the verdict. The "
"summary records the evidence."
msgstr ""
"当新证据改变某个未关闭或已解决问题的影响时，agent 可以在同一 ID "
"下提高或降低其严重级别。机器人会更新原有的行内评论，并使用新的严重级别给出判定结果。摘要中会记录该证据。"

msgid ""
"1. When you want a deep review, ask an allowlisted reviewer to apply the `ai-review` label to your PR.\n"
"2. Read the summary comment for the verdict and the full list of findings. The agent also posts findings inline when it can attach them to a changed line.\n"
"3. Fix what is marked `MUST-FIX` and push your changes. When ready, ask an allowlisted operator to post a **top-level PR comment** starting with `/ai-review`, or post it yourself if you are on the list. Inline replies do not start a round.\n"
"4. Everything is optional: without the label your PR flow is unchanged."
msgstr ""
"1. 当你需要深度评审时，请让名单中的评审者为你的 PR 添加 `ai-review` 标签。\n"
"2. 阅读摘要评论以了解判定结果和完整的问题清单。当问题可以对应到某条变更行时，agent 还会以行内评论的形式发布。\n"
"3. 修复标记为 `MUST-FIX` 的问题并推送变更。准备好后，请名单中的操作者发布一条以 `/ai-review` 开头的**顶层 PR 评论**；如果你本人就在名单中，也可以自行发布。行内回复不会启动新一轮评审。\n"
"4. 所有步骤都是可选的：不添加标签，你的 PR 流程保持不变。"
